course: dictionary
lesson: 11202
title: Wobble: moving unsteadily
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A wobble is a movement from side to side, as if something might fall over. «The chair wobbled when Sam leaned back.» Chairs do not wobble on purpose, so the clue tells you the chair is moving unsteadily.
explain: Wobble can be a verb, when something moves: «The ladder wobbled.» It can also be a noun, when there is an unsteady movement: «The table gave a wobble.» The verb changes to wobbles, wobbled and wobbling.
explain: Wobble can also mean feeling unsure for a moment: «He had a wobble before his first race.» Nobody falls over here. Try the meaning in the sentence: "He felt unsure for a moment before his first race." If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Wobble means to move unsteadily from side to side, as if about to fall.
fact: «A wobbly tooth» is a loose tooth that moves when you touch it.
fact: «Wobble on a bike» describes the shaky first tries when you are learning to ride.
fact: Wobbly things, such as a chair or ladder, should be fixed or not stood on.
fact: In science, «a spinning top wobbles» as it slows down.
exercise: «The loose chair wobbled when I leaned on it.» What does wobbled mean? | Stayed perfectly still | Made a loud noise | *Moved unsteadily from side to side | Turned into wood
exercise: Ella says, «I had a wobble before the test.» What does have a wobble mean here? | Fell over on the floor | Ran very fast | Ate a big breakfast | *Felt unsure for a moment
exercise: Which word names the unsteady movement in «The ladder gave a wobble»? | ladder | *wobble | gave | the
test: «Never stand on a wobbly ladder.» What does this sentence tell you to do? | *Fix it or do not stand on it | Stand on it quickly before it falls | Hang from it | Jump on it to test it
test: Why do children wobble when they first learn to ride a bike? | *Because balancing is new and takes practice | Because bikes are always broken | Because they are sleepy | Because bikes are always heavy
exam: Which sentence uses wobble to mean feeling unsure for a moment? | The tooth wobbled loose | *He had a wobble before going on stage | The top wobbled to the floor | The jelly wobbled on the plate
